<title>UK: UK Oct global trade deficit 454 mln stg.</title>
<headline>UK Oct global trade deficit 454 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Office for National Statistics issued the following data on Britain's global trade in October (in million stg, previously announced data in brackets)</p>
<p>    GLOBAL TRADE		 OCT	  SEPT    (PREL SEPT)</p>
<p>    Trade balance		-454	-1,059	 (-899)</p>
<p>    Exports		    14,621	13,966     (14,220)</p>
<p>    Imports		    15,075	15,025     (15,119)</p>
<p>    EU trade balance	    -36	  -254	  (-94)</p>
<p>    EU exports		  8,373	 8,061	(8,315)</p>
<p>    EU imports		  8,409	 8,315	(8,409)</p>
<p>    TRADE VALUE EX OIL/ERRATICS     OCT	SEPT  (PREL SEPT)</p>
<p>    Trade balance (in million stg)     -1,098  -1,512   (-1,389)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on pvs qtr (imports)  1.0%    2.0%     (2.5%)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on pvs qtr (exports)  2.5%    1.5%     (2.5%)</p>
<p>TRADE VOLUME EX OIL/ERRATICS</p>
<p>    Import volume index (base 1990) 128.3   129.8    (130.7)</p>
<p>    Export volume index (base 1990) 146.9   143.1    (145.7)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on pvs qtr (imports) 2.0     3.5	 (4.0%)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on yr-ago qtr (imps) 7.0     8.5	 (9.0%)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on pvs qtr (exports) 3.0     2.0	 (3.0%)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on yr-ago qtr (exps) 9.0     6.5	 (7.7%)</p>
<p>    TRADE IN OIL (VALUE MLN STG)	OCT     SEPT  (PREL SEPT)</p>
<p>    BALANCE				   448     350	(379)</p>
<p>    EXPORTS				   987     795	(825)</p>
<p>    IMPORTS				   539     445	(446)</p>
<p>Economists had forecast a deficit of 659 million stg.</p>
<p>The ONS said the erratic pattern of the deficit makes estimation of the trend difficult but said the latest estimate suggests the whole worlds goods deficit is narrowing.</p>
</text>
